# {{ name }}: Claude's working notes

A content plugin for the [Agentic Community College (ACC)](https://github.com/contract-hero/agentic-community-college) framework. **No runtime code here.** The framework owns that.

## What you can do here

- **Author a new lesson.** Do not write files by hand. Invoke ACC's `lesson-creator` skill (`/agentic-community-college:create-lesson`) and point it at this repo, a topic, and its docs. The skill emits the whole `lessons/<slug>/` tree.
- **Refine an existing lesson.** Edit `lessons/<slug>/{lesson.json, chapters.json, chapters/*.md, docs/, description.md, reference-app/}` directly. Re-run the lesson-creator validation pass after edits so `validation.json` stays true.
- **Add or refine a probe.** Edit `accContent.probes` in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`. Four kinds: `filesystem-exists`, `http-get`, `shell-exit-zero`, `claude-plugin-enabled`. The full shape lives in ACC's `mcp/server/src/schemas/courseProbes.ts`.

## What NOT to do here

- Do not add MCP server code, agents, or framework skills. Those live in `agentic-community-college`.
- Do not add top-level `agents/` or `skills/` directories. This is content only, plus the single `commands/start.md` wrapper.

## Lesson layout

```
lessons/<slug>/
├── lesson.json          slug, title, summary, prerequisites, docs, workspace { host, host_install_command, verification_cwd, solution_files, files }
├── description.md
├── docs/                curated docs snapshot + INDEX.md
├── chapters.json        schema_version 2; chapters[] with id, title, brief_md, key_idea, expected_files, tests, verification; final_verification
├── chapters/NN-<id>.md  What we implement / Done when / Implementation notes
├── reference-app/       complete solution INCLUDING every test (unit + e2e)
└── validation.json
```

The workspace seed is `reference-app/` minus `solution_files`. The learner's copy holds scaffold and tests, never the solution.

## Probe declaration cheat sheet

```json
{
  "id": "kebab-case-id",
  "kind": "shell-exit-zero",
  "message_pass": "Tool installed.",
  "message_fail": "Install <tool> from <url>.",
  "params": { "command": "tool", "args": ["--version"] },
  "remediation": { "kind": "shell", "command": "brew install tool", "timeout_ms": 60000 }
}
```

Probe ids are unique within this course. Lessons reference them in `lesson.json:prerequisites`. The course-engine runs each via `runPreflightProbe` between `selectLesson` and `setPersonalization`.

## How a session runs

1. User runs `/{{ name }}:start` from their `projectRoot`.
2. ACC's `course-engine` calls `start`: discovers this plugin, validates every lesson manifest pair and the probes block, renders the catalog, and reports the active output style. If it is not `Concise`, the skill offers `setOutputStyle`.
3. User picks a namespaced slug. `selectLesson` mints v5 state and seeds the workspace.
4. The course-engine runs the lesson's prerequisites via `runPreflightProbe`, asking before any remediation.
5. User answers personalization. `setPersonalization` persists it (`{}` accepts defaults).
6. The `course-conductor` agent loops: `nextChapter`, tell, implement until the chapter's verification passes, write the chapter artifact, `verifyChapter`, pause.
7. After the last chapter, `verifyChapter` runs `final_verification` (the e2e) and the conductor writes the summary artifact.

ACC's 8 MCP tools: `start`, `runPreflightProbe`, `selectLesson`, `setPersonalization`, `setOutputStyle`, `nextChapter`, `verifyChapter`, `configureWorkspace`.
